    text: "Round D: both Linux jobs in run 43725955802 exceeded the 30-minute limit. Logs show exhaustive native power/crash images still ran at quick depth; timeout cancellation then removed gate scratch and caused secondary ENOENT failures. Quick now executes the deterministic generated cut prefix (one tenth, at least 25), retaining complete trace/image enumeration comparisons and every original full-depth cut in deep. Completion counts and timing averages use selected outcomes only. Linked tests passed 22/22, no skips (305716 ms), including actual obliterate-packed recovery of 54/538 crash images across 832 native boundaries. Linked typecheck, build:test and lint passed. Strict unique-key YAML parsed nine files. Fixed fractional timeout rounding and validated fixture scale before spawn; disposable reverts fail both regressions and restore passes. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63qwPz is valid: docs table and cheap-path prose now include Linux self-host, identity, packed privacy and date gates. Memory-backed acceleration was measured without establishing an improvement and was discarded. No covered source was edited; unchanged 100 percent quick coverage and sub-30-minute total duration still need exact-head CI. Stage these final records, regenerate selfhost.bundle, commit it and verify committed source equality before pushing. No review-thread actions or merge."
