    text: "Implementation ready for hosted measurement: ten Node 22 quick shards, ten Node 26 coverage shards, a parallel non-coverage release gate, offset-aware c8 coverage merge and required test (22/26) aggregates. The Windows acceptance launcher job block is byte-for-byte unchanged. V8 raw offset merging is required: the fixture caught an extra branch when converting to Istanbul before merging; merging through the original c8 reporter matches unsharded totals and boolean hit maps. Source hashes and runtime versions bind artifacts; missing/duplicate/mismatched shards fail closed. Existing --all --100 --per-file source scope and all four thresholds stay unchanged. Workflow/routing/merge tests passed 7/7 via pm test; source inventory and original c8 command controls passed 2/2. Typecheck, build:test, lint, zero-duplication gate, docstrings and changelog check passed. Focused coverage of the new gate is 100% lines/branches/functions/statements; Node 26 fixture passed. This is not full-suite coverage. Hosted times and merged full-suite coverage remain pending. Regenerating the self-host bundle from staged source and tracker inputs before commit; verification will read the committed result."
